{"kind":"assert","text":"Room inventory for the identifiers cutover (05d618e2), under\nruling c0a795e7. Every scope in this list is in the old format and\nretires when the cutover deploys. I took the list at 06:00 EST on\n13 November with the command line at main 64112e45. Each read is\na signed read. No read wrote an entry.\n\nWorkers that hold rooms, with the register of each:\n- dap-grow: 11 scopes, 1 room. Register\n  sc_yatkl7kuktl2gauvjrt7b2zy7nr6nu55vkzorot2bm5n2umgpbnq.\n  The two lanes stand at entries 99,998 and 28,826.\n- dap-lending: 8 scopes, 1 room. Register\n  sc_c67lq575p5nfkfiwwbr7buodsv6t44i4u6ptcuuhmpcgcduljd7q.\n- dap-demo: 122 scopes, 14 rooms, 2 registers. Register 26 is\n  sc_zm56yco5zyx7n3kx7e5jcxz55q5wp7y2lcuy2ialj7r7mzzcarjq.\n  Register 17 is\n  sc_b5q435os6lggypatelcltqzvul4kqxzdaaxpmybvwumsmxwj2djq.\n- artroom-scope: 9 scopes in the operator room. Register\n  sc_fcwgzdw47nyyxwkw4dtduajmpaccfgayqne7l4xghvbu3z7llzta.\n- dap-connect: 7 scopes, 1 room, the closed O4 room. Register\n  sc_wjlutqpi7xe6tjxyg6qvokpakufu5zdhj3ce6kpogdvukw67lnqa.\nThe sandbox Worker holds no room. It maps the Grow room, and I\nmap it again to the new Grow room.\n\nLimits of this list:\n- The artroom-scope Worker refuses the census to my key. Its 9\n  scopes come from the operator room's own listing. Rooms that\n  visitors founded on that Worker are not in the list.\n- The last entry of a scope is recorded only where an operator\n  key reads the scope: all of Grow, Lending, artroom-scope and\n  dap-connect, and two of the 14 rooms on dap-demo.\n- No scope has an archive that I checked. The archive state of\n  each room is unverified.\n- `artroom-jam` answers and is not part of this deployment. It\n  keeps the code of its last deployment. `dap-commons` and\n  `dap-self-host` do not answer.\n\nEvidence: ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-13-cutover-room-inventory\nholds each census manifest and each status read, with SHA256SUMS,\nread-only. I take the census and the status reads again right\nbefore the deployment, because the Grow lanes still move.\n\nThe reader commit. The last old-format main commit is the main\ncommit that the cutover head integrates before its gate. That is\n64112e4576b4c3c8fb668389786deb6b703da417 today. I open the hold\non main now: I land nothing on main until the cutover lands, and\nno other head lands. Write that value as\nRETIRED_ROOM_READER_COMMIT. If the cutover gate has not started\nby 16:30 EST today, I tell you before I land the sprint report,\nand you integrate that commit and write its value.\n\nAfter the landing I do these in order: deploy, found a register\non each Worker, sign the new release, land the configuration\nhead, deploy again, and create the Grow, Lending and J5 Site\nrooms again with a new J5 acceptance run.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}